--- 3. FINDINGS AND RISK ASSESSMENT (KI-01) ---
Vulnerability ID: GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 (zod <4.6.6)
Severity: High
Path: @vercel/functions@3.10.5 -> @vercel/oidc@3.6.2 -> @vercel/cli-config@0.3.5 -> zod@<4.6.6
Classification: Transitive sub-dependency of @vercel/functions.
Application Direct Dependency: zod@3.24.4 (direct production dependency)
Available Fix: npm audit fix --force (would install breaking zod@4.6.7)
Impact: Low — The application does not use @vercel/oidc or @vercel/cli-config, and no user input or request path reaches the affected internal Vercel CLI configuration validation logic.
Decision: ACCEPTED RISK (KI-01). Per project instructions, npm audit fix --force MUST NOT be used because it forces a major breaking upgrade to Zod v4, breaking application schema validation.

